      <p>Georgetown Waterfront events run heaviest from late spring through early fall, when evening temperatures make an open-air boat genuinely pleasant and the park itself draws large after-work and weekend crowds independent of any ticketed event. That seasonal crowding compounds the parking and access problem described above — the same evening that is perfect for a sunset cruise is also the evening the waterfront park is at its most congested with joggers, tourists, and other visitors with no connection to your event at all.</p>
