      <p>On a day like this, the vehicle and driver should be almost invisible — quiet, unhurried, dignified, present exactly when needed and otherwise simply waiting without drawing attention. We brief chauffeurs specifically for funeral and memorial services differently than any other booking: appropriate dress, a measured pace, and an understanding that conversation should follow the family's lead entirely, including not at all.</p>
