      <p>The right contract structure depends on the hotel's actual booking patterns. Properties with predictable recurring group business — monthly association meetings, regular corporate clients — benefit from a scheduled shuttle run tied to known arrival and departure windows. Properties with more variable group business benefit more from an on-call account with priority dispatch and guaranteed response times during group check-in days, without committing to a fixed schedule that may not match every group's actual arrival pattern.</p>
